WEBVTT

00:33:29.958 --> 00:33:32.226
I happen to think
that those things matter.

00:33:32.250 --> 00:33:35.393
I also think, you know,

00:33:35.417 --> 00:33:39.643
why is the relationship conversation
so important at this point?

00:33:39.667 --> 00:33:42.434
And I think you can have a great job,
you can have purpose,

00:33:42.458 --> 00:33:45.393
you can have a good salary
and you can have free food,

00:33:45.417 --> 00:33:49.309
but nothing will compensate for
a poisonous relationship in the workplace,

00:33:49.333 --> 00:33:51.101
with whom you go to bed every night,

00:33:51.125 --> 00:33:53.833
fretting about somebody
who is sleeping perfectly fine.

00:33:55.125 --> 00:33:56.434
And that eats people up

00:33:56.458 --> 00:33:59.559
and that I have done for decades
in my practice.

00:33:59.583 --> 00:34:02.184
EP: It's just that I had people
come to my office